After a while, you walk through the jungle, barely catching up with the stout natives. At last, you hear the rumble and feel tremors under your feet. Soon, you reach the edge of the Wild Island. Your heart thumps because home is very close.

By an easy jump, you cross the precipice, trying not to look down. You turn around and see your guides lifting their hands up to the sky. You wave farewell to them.

Your return is right in time. Once more, the Wild Island strikes the opposite shore and stately floats away. You follow it with your eyes. Who knows if you will see it so close again in your life.

"Do you think anyone will believe us, or not?" thoughtfully asked Doyle.

"I don't know if someone will believe us, but corporal punishment is guaranteed!" you grin.

You take Snoopy by the dog leash and go home. No matter what adults and kids on the street will say, you know for sure where you've been and what you experienced. And the most important thing is, you know that you won!